{
  // DIVAN - the chancellery: it receives, records, and routes. The era after Karvansara.
  // Design authority: docs/dev/NEXT-ERA-FINDINGS-2026-08-23.md (Parts 1-5 + the Part 6 gap-fill
  // amendments), feeding on the ranked backlog of docs/dev/OBSERVABILITY-AND-MARKET-2026-08-22.md.
  // The bug sweep's own strand doc is docs/dev/DIVAN-BUG-SWEEP-2026-08-25.md.
  //
  // DECISIONS ALREADY TAKEN (owner-approved via the findings doc; do not re-litigate in-session):
  //  * Courier destination is option B (the daemon owns the token); option C (second bot) is the
  //    ESCAPE HATCH and that fork is the owner's, raised only with a measurement (findings 1.4).
  //  * A transcribed note NEVER auto-injects; promotion is an explicit button (open question 2,
  //    resolved by Part 6).
  //  * The courier serves an explicit project ALLOWLIST, not the whole StateHome catalogue
  //    (open question 3, safer default).
  //  * /cloud is owner-only first (CL-2); the engine-spawned cloud lane is a flagged experiment
  //    (CL-1) and is droppable without losing CL-2. The session loop NEVER moves to the cloud -
  //    that is a design refusal (findings Part 5), as is a cloud-cost estimate: unknown is unknown.
  //  * The inbox is NEVER committed - no .conductor/.gitignore allowlist entry; media local,
  //    pruned only by an explicit verb (open question 5, resolved by 6.1). This repo is PUBLIC.
  //  * The reporter profile (6.7) is NOT in this era - parked on the owner's keep/cut list.
  //  * Item 14 of the findings ranking (conductor verify, the Reward-Hacking Gap report) is
  //    DEFERRED to its own era, per the ranking's own note. DV6.3/DV6.4 are this plan's cut-first.
  //  * KS12.3 (ship karvansara-edge) stays the OWNER'S, untouched: the version-number call and the
  //    payesh corpus call are not this era's to take. This branch stacks on feat/karvansara-edge.
  //
  // STAGE ORDER IS DELIBERATE: DV1 (channel health + owner queue push) is the findings' own #1-#2
  // and the courier's prerequisite. DV2 sweeps the known defects BEFORE the era builds on the
  // battery seam, the Telegram service and the run-state store - the three places they live.
  // DV3 inbox before DV4 courier (the inbox works with no daemon; the daemon serves it).
  // DV5 cloud and DV6 record-out are independent; DV6 carries the two cut-first checkpoints.
  // DV7 closes the era, KS10/KS12 pattern, ownerGate on the ship.
  //
  // TRAPS THIS FILE ITSELF CARRIES (inherited, all still true):
  //  * `conductor plan set` round-trips this file through System.Text.Json and DROPS EVERY COMMENT.
  //    This annotated copy is the master; restore comments by hand after any live edit.
  //  * `agent.model` is dropped silently unless "{model}" appears in BOTH args and resumeArgs. It does.
  //    Verify with `conductor journey` - the Model column must never read (default).
  //  * templatesDir resolves against THIS FILE'S directory: "templates" means plans/divan/templates/.
  //    tracker and planDoc are repo-relative. They differ on purpose; do not "fix" one to match.
  //  * limits.maxSessionTokens and softBreakRatio are MEASURED, not guessed: 35M / 0.90 is the
  //    prescription KS12.1 wrote into docs/dev/TOKEN-BUDGET-TUNING.md section 12 from `budget`'s own
  //    verdict on the edge run (nudge 31.5M clears the 29.4M largest closer; headroom 3.5M is 2.0x
  //    the 1.74M measured wrap-up). Valid for claude-opus-5 on THIS repo only; any model change
  //    re-derives before launch.
  //  * Cap $420 = est $318 (23 cp x $13.81, the edge era's honest measured figure) + ~32% headroom,
  //    the same policy the edge cap used.
  //  * CORRECTED IN PLACE AT DV7.1 (2026-08-26), measured, not re-estimated - see TOKEN-BUDGET-TUNING
  //    section 13. The two claims above were both optimistic and the LIMITS ARE DELIBERATELY LEFT
  //    UNCHANGED: this run is mid-flight and trap 14 forbids moving its ceiling. What is corrected is
  //    what the next plan copies from here.
  //    - the $13.81/cp basis: outturn is $14.45/cp over 20 checkpoints ($289.04). Projected 23 cp =
  //      ~$332, still inside 420, so the cap policy held. The BASIS did not - it was 4.6% low, and
  //      edge's was 4.3% low on karvan's. Two eras short in the same direction: next plan uses
  //      19M / $14.50 per checkpoint and treats it as a floor.
  //    - the 35M/0.90 pair: the edge prescription justified it as "headroom 3.5M is 2.0x the 1.74M
  //      measured wrap-up". Divan's own wrap-up measured 2.42M, so the real headroom was 1.4x - under
  //      the >=1.5x rule the whole era, and the largest closer came in at 35.29M against a 35M cap.
  //      `budget` now prescribes 42M / 0.9 (nudge 37.8M) for the NEXT era. Still claude-opus-5 only.
  //  * batteries is bounded ON PURPOSE (ledgerMaxEntries 3 / maxBytes 6144): the unbounded ledger
  //    silently starves the open-bugs battery (DIVAN-BUG-SWEEP ledger 3, item 1) and this run
  //    depends on sessions SEEING the bug list. DV2.2 lands the engine fix; the bound stays anyway.
  "version": "1.0",
  "planVersion": 1,
  "name": "Divan - the chancellery: inbox, courier, and the record that gets out",
  "repo": "C:/code/conductor",
  // payesh is a satellite ONLY so DV7.2's harvest-refresh commits register as progress - the
  // verdict diffs it, nothing more. No stage before DV7 has any business there. Never push its
  // main: that repo auto-deploys a public site.
  "satelliteRepos": [
    "C:/code/conductor-site"
  ],
  "tracker": "plans/divan/TRACKER.md",
  "planDoc": "docs/dev/NEXT-ERA-FINDINGS-2026-08-23.md",
  "branchPattern": "^feat/divan$",
  "pauseOnBlocked": true,
  "agent": {
    "command": "claude",
    "args": [
      "-p",
      "{prompt}",
      "--output-format",
